-- Source module: Solutions.ButterflyCost
/-!
# §5.3 Batching a common layer: the cost recurrence

Normalized by the current logical volume, the paper's recurrence is
`F(e) ≤ (s/W) F(e/m) + O((eK)^τ + 1)` at internal nodes and `F(e) = O(e)` at leaves `e < d^β`.
In volume form (`T k V` = time of a node `k` levels above its leaves, of leaf width `u`, on a
stream of volume `V`; each of the `s` children runs on volume `V/W`):

`T 0 V ≤ C₀ V u`, `T (k+1) V ≤ C V (u m^{k+1})^λ + s T k (V/W)`.

* `overhead_le`: at an internal node, `(eK)^τ + 1 ≤ 2 e^λ` (since `K ≤ e^{c/β}`).
* `batch_time`: `T k V ≤ V (K₁ (u m^k)^λ + C₀ (s/W)^k u)` when `s/W < m^λ`
  (generalizes `AModel.power_width_time` to a level-dependent overhead).
* `batch_time_sigma`: with `s/W ≤ m^σ`, `(s/W)^k u ≤ e^σ u^{1-σ}`.
* `layer_total`: the base-`m` pieces plus `O(V log d)` preprocessing give `O(V d^{λ'})` for
  every `λ' > max{λ, σ + β(1-σ)}`.
-/

